                        "review": "Oriental Empires: Total War: China Before Total War: China\n\nRegret: 69% (7.01 euro per hour for a very confused emperor)\n\nOriental Empires is a strategy game set in ancient China, with a campaign map and real-time battles. It sounds like Total War, but it plays like its slower, quieter cousin. The idea is good, but the battles felt stiff and I never really knew what was happening. 5 hours in, I bought Total War: Three Kingdoms in my head instead.\n\n[hr][/hr]\n[b][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/46453681]Help me out by following my Curator, I'd really appreciate it!![/url][/b]\n",
